unavailable-subtitle: The constitutional litigation team cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; constitutional_restraint += 4; judicial_repair_mandate += 2; court_user_trust += 2; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "Lewica publishes an institutional alternative from opposition"

Lewica's lawyers file a brief against the expanded power and attach a draft
appointments statute that would bind both ministry and President. [? if
left_in_government: Coalition partners must now answer an argument from inside
their own majority, but the serving Justice Minister remains free to reject
it.?][? if not left_in_government: The government can ignore an opposition
brief; it cannot claim that no workable alternative was offered.?]

- @poland_event_queue: File the brief

@competence_opposition_record
title: Put the constitutional objection on the Sejm record
subtitle: Record a parliamentary position without pretending that Lewica controls the ministry or the President.
view-if: left_in_government = 0 or justice_minister_party != "Lewica"
on-arrival: constitutional_restraint += 1; judicial_repair_mandate += 1; news_headline = "Lewica records its objection to the Tribunal ruling in the Sejm"

The club reads its objection into the Sejm record and names the appointment
rule it would support. No vacancy is filled and no state institution changes
course. What remains is a dated position that future ministers, judges and
Lewica itself can be made to answer for.

- @poland_event_queue: Read it into the record

