Q.justice_crisis_majority = majority;
Q.justice_crisis_left_seats = leftSeats;
Q.justice_crisis_cabinet_seats = cabinetSeats;
Q.justice_crisis_without_left = Math.max(0, cabinetSeats - leftSeats);
Q.justice_crisis_gap = Math.max(
    0, majority - Q.justice_crisis_without_left
);
Q.justice_crisis_konf_seats = konfFamily;
// Whether our veto is a threat or a noise. If the cabinet parties can reach
// 231 without us, or can already talk to Konfederacja, the red line is a
// statement rather than a lever.
Q.justice_crisis_left_pivotal =
    Q.justice_crisis_gap > 0 &&
    !(Q.ko_konf_partner_line != "closed" &&
        Q.justice_crisis_without_left + konfFamily >= majority)
        ? 1 : 0;
// Who at the cabinet table would actually carry the appointment. The event only
// opens under a Prime Minister who wants him there, and beyond that only KO and
// PSL would sign it: Poland 2050 in the Council of Ministers is a standing
// objection, and without a partner willing to wear it the third name stays a
// briefing rather than a nomination.
let partnerWillingness = 1;
if (Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet) partnerWillingness += 1;
if (Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet) partnerWillingness -= 1;
Q.justice_crisis_appointment_possible = partnerWillingness >= 1 ? 1 : 0;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 14;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Chancellery opens the justice ministry after the reckoning's failures";
!}

= June 2026 — The ministry becomes the answer

**[+ prime_minister +]** has decided that the problem with the reckoning is the
ministry.

It is not a defensible diagnosis and it is an entirely predictable one.
[? if reckoning_case_outcome = "collapsed": January's flagship indictment came
back from the court in its entirety.?][? if reckoning_case_outcome = "returned":
Most of January's flagship indictment came back for supplementation.?]
[? if reckoning_case_outcome = "narrowed": One narrowed count from January's
flagship indictment is at trial, which is more than anyone expected and far
less than what was promised.?] The prosecution service is still staffed by the
people it was staffed by in 2023. The courts that would convict are courts this
government calls defective. The President signs nothing that would repair
either. None of that fits on a card, and *a new justice minister* does.

[? if reckoning_case_response = "Blame the ministry": In January we joined the
attack on the ministry ourselves. The Chancellery's briefers are quoting us
back at our own ministers this week, accurately.?]
[? if reckoning_route = "Independent prosecution statute": Our 2025 statute did
change one thing permanently: the Prosecutor General is no longer the justice
minister. Whoever takes this office inherits courts, prisons and legislation,
and cannot lift a telephone about a named case.?]

**[+ justice_crisis_incumbent +]** is being removed for the pace of a process
that the removal will not accelerate. The question in front of us is not
whether that is fair. It is who arrives instead.

- @justice_crisis_names: See the three names on the Chancellery's list

@justice_crisis_names
title: The three names
on-arrival: {!
Q.news_headline =
    "Three names circulate for the justice ministry: continuity, a judge, and Giertych";
!}

= The list

**[+ justice_crisis_incumbent +]** — the incumbent. Careful, institutional,
disliked by the coalition's own militants for exactly the reasons the
Commission likes him. Kept in office, he continues doing slowly what can be
done lawfully, and the government continues being attacked for it every week
until the election.

**Waldemar Żurek** — a judge of the Kraków regional court and, for years, the
spokesman of the old National Council of the Judiciary. He was the face of the
judges who refused to accept the 2017 reconstruction, and he paid for it with
disciplinary proceedings, transfers between divisions and a decade of
harassment. He is a KO nominee and not a KO politician. He would arrive with
the authority of the people PiS spent eight years punishing, and with no
apparatus of his own inside the ministry.

**Roman Giertych** — chairman of the reckoning team, deputy for Kielce, and the
man the Prime Minister actually trusts. He would arrive promising the thing the
Chancellery wants to be able to say before the election: that somebody is
finally moving. He would also arrive as the former leader of the League of
Polish Families and the deputy prime minister who ran the campaign against
so-called homosexual propaganda in Polish schools, into a cabinet containing
this party.

= What our votes are worth this week

The cabinet parties hold **[+ justice_crisis_cabinet_seats +]** seats of **[+
sejm_total +]**. Ours are **[+ justice_crisis_left_seats +]** of them. Without
us the cabinet has **[+ justice_crisis_without_left +]**, against a majority of
**[+ justice_crisis_majority +]**.

[? if justice_crisis_gap > 0: They are **[+ justice_crisis_gap +]** short. That
is the whole of our leverage and it is real.?]
[? if justice_crisis_gap = 0: They are not short. The cabinet parties can pass
what they like without a single Left vote, which means every sentence we say
this week is a request.?]
[? if justice_crisis_left_pivotal = 0 and justice_crisis_gap > 0: Konfederacja
holds **[+ justice_crisis_konf_seats +]**, and KO's channel to it is already
open. The gap can be closed without us, and everyone at the coalition table has
done that arithmetic before we walked in.?]
[? if justice_crisis_left_pivotal = 1: Konfederacja holds **[+
justice_crisis_konf_seats +]**, and the door to it is formally closed. For as
long as it stays closed, a cabinet without us is a cabinet without a
majority.?]

= Who at the table would sign it

The third name is not the Prime Minister's alone. A minister is appointed by
the President on the Prime Minister's motion, and a coalition cabinet's motions
are cleared at the coalition council first.

[? if justice_crisis_appointment_possible = 1: **[+ prime_minister +]** wants
him and has somewhere to get the signature. [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1:
PSL will not spend anything to stop a national-conservative taking Justice; a
former League of Polish Families leader is not the kind of appointment its
deputies lose sleep over.?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0: There is no
partner at this table with an institutional objection to him and the standing to
press it.?] The nomination is available if we do not make it expensive.?]
[? if justice_crisis_appointment_possible = 0: Poland 2050 sits in this Council
of Ministers and has spent three years describing itself as the party of
institutional decency. Its ministers will not put their names on a motion
appointing him, and **[+ prime_minister +]** cannot present a motion his own
cabinet will not clear. The third name is a briefing, not a nomination — which
means our red line, if we draw one, will be free, and will look far braver than
it was.?]

**[+ ko_leader +]** wants an answer before Thursday's coalition council.

- @jc_save
- @jc_zurek
- @jc_veto
- @jc_abstain

@jc_save
