= A judge takes the ministry

We do not defend the incumbent and we do not wait to be presented with a name.
We put **Waldemar Żurek** on the table first, and we put him there with PSL and
the centre already agreeing, so that refusing him would mean the Prime Minister
publicly preferring a politician to the judge PiS spent eight years punishing.

He is sworn in within the fortnight. He arrives with moral authority, a
complete absence of party apparatus and no power whatever over the appeal
timetable of a single case. The Chancellery gets its announcement. The
reckoning gets a minister who will be believed when he explains why something
is impossible.

**Giertych** does not get the ministry, and knows precisely who arranged that.
He remains chairman of the team, in the Sejm, with a portfolio of grievance and
two years to use it.

- @poland_event_queue: Attend the swearing-in

@jc_veto
title: State the red line in public: not in a cabinet with him
subtitle: The strongest thing we can say and the last thing we can say. If KO can count to 231 without us, it becomes a bluff in the same week we make it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.justice_crisis_response = "Public red line";
// The veto works only while the cabinet parties actually need our votes and
// KO's own centre of gravity has not moved past the point of caring. It is
// also unnecessary where no partner would sign the appointment anyway.
const vetoHolds =
    Q.justice_crisis_appointment_possible != 1 ||
    (Q.justice_crisis_left_pivotal == 1 &&
        (Number(Q.ko_right_score) || 50) < 60 &&
        (Number(Q.giertych_standing) || 46) < 66);
Q.giertych_justice_outcome = vetoHolds
    ? ((Number(Q.reckoning_pm_pressure) || 0) >= 40 ? "zurek" : "incumbent")
    : "giertych";
Q.progressive_credibility += 8;
Q.razem_cooperation += 6;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 6;
Q.feminist_trust += 4;
Q.ko_relation -= 10;
Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 8;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 8;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.3;
if (Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "zurek") {
    Q.justice_minister = "Waldemar Żurek";
    Q.justice_minister_party = "KO";
    Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 4;
    Q.reckoning_pm_pressure = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.reckoning_pm_pressure) || 0) - 10
    );
}
if (Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "giertych") {
    Q.giertych_standing = Math.min(
        100, (Number(Q.giertych_standing) || 46) + 10
    );
} else {
    Q.giertych_standing = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.giertych_standing) || 46) - 14
    );
}
Q.news_headline = Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "giertych"
    ? "The Left's red line is published and the Chancellery crosses it"
    : "The Left's red line holds and Giertych does not get the ministry";
!}

= The line, and what is on the other side of it

**Anna Maria Żukowska** says it from the club rostrum with the dates attached,
and **[+ left_leader +]** confirms it in the same hour so that nobody can call
it one deputy's temperament: this party will not sit in a Council of Ministers
that contains Roman Giertych. Not as an objection, not as a preference — as the
condition of our participation.

[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "incumbent": The arithmetic answers before the
Chancellery does. **[+ justice_crisis_gap +]** seats cannot be found anywhere
that KO is willing to look, and a coalition council that has just been told the
price does not test it. **[+ justice_crisis_incumbent +]** stays in office and
the reshuffle quietly becomes a reshuffle of two deputy ministers. We have
converted a threat into a fact, once. It will not be as frightening the second
time.?]
[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "zurek": The Chancellery cannot cross the line
and cannot be seen to retreat, so it does what governments do: it produces a
third name. **Waldemar Żurek** is announced within the week, and every briefer
explains that this was always the plan. The Prime Minister gets his change, we
get a judge instead of a party lawyer, and the red line is now a published
document that both sides pretend was never tested.?]
[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "giertych": The Chancellery answers on
Thursday. It has counted, and the count is that our line is a sentence. The
nomination goes to the President with Giertych's name on it, and KO's press
office spends the afternoon explaining that a coalition partner does not
appoint another party's ministers. We have said the most serious thing a
governing party can say, in public, with dates. Now we have to mean it.?]

- @justice_crisis_close

@jc_abstain
title: Refuse to bargain over another party's ministry
subtitle: Say that KO appoints KO's ministers, spend nothing, and let the Chancellery's own balance decide who walks into the building.
on-arrival: {!
Q.justice_crisis_response = "No position";
// Nothing is spent, so nothing is bought: KO's own right-hand drift, the
// chairman's standing and the Prime Minister's panic decide the appointment.
const koRight = Number(Q.ko_right_score) || 50;
const standing = Number(Q.giertych_standing) || 46;
const pressure = Number(Q.reckoning_pm_pressure) || 0;
Q.giertych_justice_outcome =
    Q.justice_crisis_appointment_possible == 1 &&
    (koRight >= 56 || standing >= 58 || (Number(Q.ko_relation) || 0) < 30) &&
        pressure >= 30
        ? "giertych"
        : pressure >= 26 ? "zurek" : "incumbent";
Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
Q.razem_dissent += 5;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 4;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.public_trust -= 1;
if (Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "zurek") {
    Q.justice_minister = "Waldemar Żurek";
    Q.justice_minister_party = "KO";
    Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 3;
}
if (Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "giertych") {
    Q.giertych_standing = Math.min(
        100, (Number(Q.giertych_standing) || 46) + 8
    );
}
Q.news_headline = Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "giertych"
    ? "The Left takes no position and the Chancellery appoints Giertych"
    : Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "zurek"
        ? "The Left takes no position and a judge takes the justice ministry"
        : "The Left takes no position and the justice minister survives";
!}

= Somebody else's ministry

We say the constitutionally impeccable thing: the Prime Minister proposes
ministers, coalition partners do not veto each other's personnel, and Lewica
will judge the office by what comes out of it. Then we go back to the housing
committee.

[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "incumbent": Nothing happens. The Chancellery
looks at the same three names without anybody pushing, decides that a
reshuffle it cannot present as a success is worse than no reshuffle, and keeps
**[+ justice_crisis_incumbent +]**. We spent nothing and received the outcome we
would have paid for, which will make us worse at estimating this next time.?]
[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "zurek": Without anybody in the room arguing
for a politician, the Prime Minister takes the safe name. **Waldemar Żurek** is
sworn in. It is the result we wanted, produced by a coalition dynamic we had no
part in, and our own deputies notice that we were not the reason.?]
[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "giertych": In a room where nobody has said no,
the Prime Minister appoints the man he trusts. Our silence is entered in the
minutes as consent, because in a coalition council that is what silence is. By
Friday the nomination is at the Palace.?]

- @justice_crisis_close

@justice_crisis_close
title: [? if giertych_justice_outcome = "giertych": Follow the nomination to the Palace?][? if giertych_justice_outcome != "giertych": Record the appointment and leave the council?]
go-to: giertych_appointment_2026 if giertych_justice_outcome = "giertych"; poland_event_queue

@giertych_appointment_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The swearing-in is a scene rather than a state change, the coalition's arithmetic without us is computed and printed before the decision, and both branches carry their real price: an unsurvivable internal cost, or a minority cabinet whose next majority we do not control.
title: Giertych is sworn in
subtitle: The far right's former education minister takes the Ministry of Justice in a cabinet containing this party
face-image: img/poland/events/presidential-palace-interior.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.giertych_justice_outcome = "giertych";
Q.giertych_in_government = 1;
