Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 12;
Q.news_headline = Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "giertych"
    ? "Roman Giertych is appointed Minister of Justice"
    : Q.giertych_justice_outcome == "zurek"
        ? "Waldemar Żurek is appointed Minister of Justice"
        : "The justice minister survives the Prime Minister's patience";
!}

= June 2026 — A ministry changes hands without us

**[+ prime_minister +]** has decided that the reason nothing has been convicted
is the ministry, which is not true and is announceable. Three names circulate:
**[+ justice_crisis_incumbent +]**, the incumbent; **Waldemar Żurek**, the
Kraków judge who was the face of the resistance to the 2017 reconstruction and
paid for it in disciplinary proceedings; and **Roman Giertych**, chairman of the
reckoning team, the Prime Minister's own lawyer, and the deputy prime minister
who ran the campaign against so-called homosexual propaganda in Polish schools.

We are outside this cabinet. We do not hold a vote on any of them, we cannot
condition a coalition we are not in, and what we say now is a standard we will
be measured against rather than a veto.

[? if justice_crisis_appointment_possible = 0: One thing does constrain it
without us. Poland 2050 sits in this Council of Ministers and will not clear a
motion appointing him, so the third name cannot reach the President however
much **[+ prime_minister +]** wants it to.?]
[? if justice_crisis_appointment_possible = 1: Nothing at that table
constrains it. [? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 1: PSL has no objection it is
willing to spend anything on.?][? if ministry_psl_in_cabinet = 0: There is no
partner left with both an institutional objection and the standing to press
it.?]?]

[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "giertych": By Friday the nomination is
Giertych's. The far right's former education minister takes the Ministry of
Justice, and this time nobody had to be persuaded to sit beside him.?]
[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "zurek": By Friday the nomination is Żurek's.
The Chancellery gets a change it can announce and a minister nobody can
plausibly call a party appointment.?]
[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "incumbent": By Friday there is no nomination.
The Prime Minister discovers that a reshuffle he cannot present as a success is
worse than no reshuffle, and **[+ justice_crisis_incumbent +]** stays.?]

- @jc_opp_standard
- @jc_opp_statute
- @jc_opp_campaign

@jc_opp_standard
title: Publish the standard this office has to meet, name by name
subtitle: Say now what would disqualify a nominee, so that it cannot be written after the appointment to fit it.
on-arrival: giertych_line = "Published disqualification standard"; progressive_credibility += 6; institutional_trust += 3; public_trust += 2; judicial_legitimacy += 2; ko_relation -= 4; giertych_standing -= 5; news_headline = "Lewica publishes the standard it will hold the justice ministry to"

We publish it before the name is announced: what the office requires, what
disqualifies, and the specific record — circulars, dates, ministry
correspondence — that we say disqualifies one of the three. Then we say we will
apply the same test to our own nominee if we ever hold it.

It is the only kind of authority available to a party with no votes in the
question: having said it first, in writing, while it could still have been
wrong.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the standard

@jc_opp_statute
title: Offer the government's votes for an independent prosecution statute
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Make the office matter less, permanently, instead of arguing about who holds it.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no free capacity to draft and whip an independent-prosecution bill from opposition.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.giertych_line = "Opposition prosecution statute";
// A government that has just appointed a clean-looking minister cannot refuse
// the bill that would make him so. One that appointed Giertych can, and does.
if (Q.giertych_justice_outcome != "giertych") {
    Q.prosecutor_general_separated = 1;
}
Q.prosecution_independence += 8;
Q.prosecution_command_clarity += 5;
Q.constitutional_restraint += 5;
Q.institutional_trust += 4;
Q.judicial_legitimacy += 3;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.giertych_standing = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.giertych_standing) || 46) - 6
);
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica offers opposition votes to take the prosecution service out of the ministry";
!}

We table the statute we would have tabled in government: a fixed-term Prosecutor
General, transparent removal, every instruction about a named case written down
and published. We offer the votes to pass it and we offer them to whoever holds
the ministry, which is the point.

[? if giertych_justice_outcome = "giertych": The government will not take it
this month, for the obvious reason. It is on the order paper with our names on
it, and it will still be there when the first instruction becomes public.?]
[? if giertych_justice_outcome != "giertych": The government takes it, because
a minister appointed to look clean cannot refuse the bill that would make him
so. The office we were arguing about becomes a smaller office.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Table the statute

@jc_opp_campaign
title: Make the appointment the campaign
subtitle: The clearest attack available and the one that concedes the institutional argument entirely.
on-arrival: giertych_line = "Appointment campaign"; media_capacity += 6; left_poll_momentum += 0.4; ko_poll_momentum -= 0.3; progressive_credibility += 4; feminist_trust += 4; ko_relation -= 9; institutional_trust -= 2; reckoning_noise += 8; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 6; news_headline = "The Left turns the justice appointment into a national campaign"

The 2006 circulars go on every screen beside the swearing-in photograph, and
the teachers disciplined under his ministry are given the microphone rather than
our spokespeople. It is the strongest week of opposition media this party has
had all year.

It also settles nothing about prosecutors, courts, appeal timetables or the
files themselves, and it teaches the coalition that our objection is about a
biography rather than an office. The next appointment will be defended on that
basis, and the defence will work.

- @poland_event_queue: Run the campaign

