Q.far_right_agenda += 2;
Q.minority_safety += 2;
Q.government_delivery += 2;
Q.institutional_trust += 2;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 4;
Q.news_headline =
    "Dariusz Piontkowski takes the deputy premiership PiS wanted for Czarnek";
!}

= A deputy premiership with nobody's programme in it

We concede the rank, because the rank is what the leadership actually needs, and
we spend the week making sure it goes to somebody with no movement behind him.
**Dariusz Piontkowski** was education minister before Czarnek was: an
administrator, a school-network man, a person with opinions about staffing
tables and none he would resign over.

He is sworn in with the coordinating brief. The committee he chairs will be
slow, procedural and largely uninterested in what our ministers put in front of
it, which is the best outcome available from a table where we hold no veto over
anybody's personnel.

**Czarnek** keeps the caucus current, the television bookings and a grievance
with our fingerprints on it. He is now the most obvious alternative to a
leadership that passed him over to keep us, and everyone in that party knows who
arranged it.

- @poland_event_queue: Attend the swearing-in

@cc_veto
title: State the red line: not in a Council of Ministers with him
subtitle: Say what our members have been waiting two and a half years to hear, and find out in the same week whether the arithmetic behind it is real.
on-arrival: {!
Q.culture_crisis_response = "Public red line";
// The veto is a lever only while the cabinet needs us — which, on this path,
// means only while the United Right cannot be reassembled behind our backs.
const vetoHolds =
    Q.culture_crisis_appointment_possible != 1 ||
    (Q.culture_crisis_left_pivotal == 1 &&
        (Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 32) < 58 &&
        (Number(Q.culture_current_standing) || 44) < 64);
Q.czarnek_office_outcome = vetoHolds
    ? ((Number(Q.culture_current_pressure) || 0) >= 52
        ? "piontkowski" : "blocked")
    : "czarnek";
Q.progressive_credibility += 10;
Q.razem_cooperation += 7;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 8;
Q.razem_dissent -= 7;
Q.feminist_trust += 5;
Q.minority_safety += 4;
Q.pis_relation -= 12;
Q.government_coalition_dissent += 10;
Q.left_poll_momentum += 0.35;
if (Q.czarnek_office_outcome == "piontkowski") {
    Q.deputy_pm_social_brief = "Dariusz Piontkowski";
    Q.culture_current_pressure = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.culture_current_pressure) || 0) - 10
    );
}
if (Q.czarnek_office_outcome == "czarnek") {
    Q.culture_current_standing = Math.min(
        100, (Number(Q.culture_current_standing) || 44) + 10
    );
} else {
    Q.culture_current_standing = Math.max(
        0, (Number(Q.culture_current_standing) || 44) - 15
    );
}
Q.news_headline = Q.czarnek_office_outcome == "czarnek"
    ? "The Left's red line is published and PiS crosses it"
    : "The Left's red line holds and Czarnek does not enter the cabinet";
!}

= The line, and what is on the other side of it

**Anna Maria Żukowska** reads the 2019 quotation into the record with the date
and the programme it was broadcast on, and **[+ left_leader +]** confirms it
within the hour so that it cannot be filed as one deputy's temper: this party
will not sit in a Council of Ministers that contains Przemysław Czarnek. Not an
objection. The condition of our participation.

For the first time in two and a half years, our own regional organisations
publish supportive statements without being asked.

[? if czarnek_office_outcome = "blocked": The arithmetic answers before the
Chancellery does. **[+ culture_crisis_gap +]** seats cannot be found anywhere
this leadership is currently able to look, and a coalition council that has just
been shown the price does not test it. The nomination is withdrawn. We have
converted a threat into a fact, once, and made it slightly less frightening the
next time.?]
[? if czarnek_office_outcome = "piontkowski": The leadership cannot cross the
line and cannot be seen to retreat, so it produces a third name. **Dariusz
Piontkowski** takes the deputy premiership within the week and every briefer
explains that this was always the intention. The rank is conceded, the movement
is not, and the red line becomes a published document both sides pretend was
never tested.?]
[? if czarnek_office_outcome = "czarnek": PiS answers on Thursday. It has
counted, and the count is that our line is a sentence. The nomination goes to
the President with Czarnek's name on it, and the party that spent thirty months
being called soft by Ziobro spends one afternoon being called something else.
We have said the most serious thing a governing party can say, in public, with
dates. Now we have to mean it.?]

- @culture_crisis_close

@cc_abstain
title: Refuse to bargain over another party's personnel
subtitle: The position we have taken on every PiS appointment since we signed. It has been defensible every time, and this is the appointment it was always going to have to cover.
on-arrival: {!
Q.culture_crisis_response = "No position";
const rightAgenda = Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 32;
const standing = Number(Q.culture_current_standing) || 44;
const pressure = Number(Q.culture_current_pressure) || 0;
Q.czarnek_office_outcome =
    Q.culture_crisis_appointment_possible == 1 &&
    (rightAgenda >= 44 || standing >= 56 || (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) < 30) &&
        pressure >= 40
        ? "czarnek"
        : pressure >= 34 ? "piontkowski" : "blocked";
Q.progressives_dissent += 9;
Q.razem_dissent += 10;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 8;
Q.coalition_blur += 6;
Q.pis_relation += 3;
Q.public_trust -= 2;
if (Q.czarnek_office_outcome == "piontkowski") {
    Q.deputy_pm_social_brief = "Dariusz Piontkowski";
}
if (Q.czarnek_office_outcome == "czarnek") {
    Q.culture_current_standing = Math.min(100, standing + 8);
}
Q.news_headline = Q.czarnek_office_outcome == "czarnek"
    ? "The Left takes no position and PiS appoints Czarnek"
    : Q.czarnek_office_outcome == "piontkowski"
        ? "The Left takes no position and a departmental administrator takes the rank"
        : "The Left takes no position and the nomination lapses";
!}

= Somebody else's personnel

We say the thing we have said about every PiS appointment since December 2023:
that the Prime Minister proposes ministers, that coalition partners do not veto
each other's people, and that we will judge the office by what comes out of it.
Then we go back to the housing committee.

It was a defensible position when the appointment was a deputy minister for
water management.

[? if czarnek_office_outcome = "blocked": Nothing happens. Without anybody in
the room forcing the question, the leadership decides that a promotion it cannot
present as a triumph is worth less than the argument, and the nomination lapses.
We spent nothing and received what we would have paid for, which will make us
worse at estimating this next time.?]
[? if czarnek_office_outcome = "piontkowski": Without a fight to win, the
leadership takes the safe name and **Dariusz Piontkowski** gets the rank. It is
the result we wanted, produced by a party dynamic we had no part in, and our own
deputies notice that we were not the reason.?]
[? if czarnek_office_outcome = "czarnek": In a room where nobody has said no,
the leadership appoints the man its base has been demanding for thirty months.
Our silence is entered in the minutes as consent, because in a coalition council
that is what silence is. By Friday the nomination is at the Palace.?]

- @culture_crisis_close

@culture_crisis_close
