= June 2026 — Column Hall

The President administers the oath and the photographers get the frame they came
for: **Przemysław Czarnek** with his hand raised, and behind him the Council of
Ministers of a government this party belongs to.

Teachers disciplined under his ministry are on air by lunchtime. So are the
organisations that were audited into closure while Willa Plus money went to
foundations with the right addresses. The 2019 sentence is played on a loop,
and every broadcast of it is now, technically, a broadcast about a member of a
cabinet in which we sit.

Our equality deputies are asked, one after another and on camera, whether the
Deputy Prime Minister thinks they are equal to normal people. There is no answer
to that question available to someone who has not resigned.

[? if formation_pis_left_safeguards >= 2: The safeguards hold, and they matter:
the equality and institutional clauses are enforceable, they bind him, and his
committee cannot amend them by circular. Every one of those clauses was written
for a day exactly like this one, and none of them prevents him from chairing the
committee our ministers report to.?]
[? if formation_pis_left_safeguards < 2: We signed too few safeguards for any of
them to bind him. The committee he chairs clears our ministers' circulars, and
there is no clause in the contract that says what happens when it refuses.?]

= The arithmetic, before anybody says anything they cannot withdraw

The cabinet parties hold **[+ culture_crisis_cabinet_seats +]**. Ours are **[+
culture_crisis_left_seats +]**. Without us: **[+ culture_crisis_without_left +]**
against **[+ culture_crisis_majority +]**[? if culture_crisis_gap > 0: — **[+
culture_crisis_gap +]** short?][? if culture_crisis_gap = 0: — a majority?].

[? if culture_crisis_gap > 0: If we go, this becomes a minority cabinet on the
day it swears in the man it lost its right flank to replace. It does not fall:
removing it needs 231 votes for a named successor, and dissolving this Sejm
needs 307 of 460. What it becomes is a government that has to buy a majority —
and there are **[+ culture_crisis_right_reserve +]** seats sitting on the right
of this chamber that used to belong to the same bloc.
[? if united_right_return_blocked = 1: Our no-return clause is what stands
between this cabinet and them. It is a clause in a contract with a partner that
has just crossed our red line.?]?]
[? if culture_crisis_gap = 0: If we go, nothing arithmetical happens. The
cabinet keeps its majority and loses the only partner that ever made it look
like something other than the United Right with better manners.?]

Two doors, and no third one that leaves both this government and this party
where they were on Wednesday.

- @pis_rupture_stay
- @pis_rupture_break

