    0, (Number(Q.early_election_risk) || 0) - 14
);
Q.government_coalition_dissent = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.government_coalition_dissent) || 0) - 8
);
Q.far_right_agenda = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 32) - 5);
Q.konf_normalisation = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.konf_normalisation) || 0) - 4
);
Q.pis_relation += 6;
Q.institutional_trust += 3;
Q.government_delivery += 2;
Q.minority_safety += 3;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 9;
Q.razem_dissent += 14;
Q.progressives_dissent += 10;
Q.coalition_blur += 7;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left supplies a PiS minority bill by bill to keep the United Right apart";
!}

We publish the terms rather than negotiate them privately: the enacted social
floor is not reopened, the wage and housing bills go through in the form we
wrote them, no vote of ours is traded for a personnel decision, and every vote
we supply is announced with its price the day before.

The cabinet survives, and Ziobro and Mentzen stay outside, because a government
that can reach 231 through us has no reason to pay what they are asking. That is
the entire argument for doing this, and it is a real one.

It is also a party that resigned over a Deputy Prime Minister on Tuesday and
kept his government alive on Thursday. Razem says exactly that sentence, in
public, and there is no answer to it except the count of what the published
terms actually save.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the terms

@pis_posture_snap
title: Refuse supply and demand that this Sejm end itself
subtitle: The honest position, and the one the constitution makes hardest: dissolution needs 307 votes and nobody has counted them.
